{
  "UniqueID": "water_sawmill_mill_race_outlet_closed",
  "CardName": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_mill_race_outlet_closed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_MillRaceOutletClosed_CardName",
    "DefaultText": "Mill Race Outlet (Closed)"
  },
  "CardDescription": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_mill_race_outlet_closed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_MillRaceOutletClosed_CardDescription",
    "DefaultText": "The outlet's valve is shut and no water flows from it: nothing can be drawn, a Rain Cistern here is not fed, and stations that need this outlet's water stop. Open the valve to let the water run again."
  },
  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_mill_race_outlet_closed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_MillRaceOutletClosed_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Closed:</b> The valve is shut, so no water can be drawn, a Rain Cistern here is not fed, and the stations here that run on this outlet stop and no new station can be built on it. A station at a river or lake, or beside another open outlet, keeps working. Heat does not count a closed outlet as running, the way it does a frozen one.\n\n<b>Open Valve:</b> Let the water run again (15 minutes). The outlet then draws, feeds its cistern and freezes in winter as before.\n\n<b>Seasons:</b> A closed outlet does not freeze or thaw.\n\n<b>Pack Up:</b> Recover the outlet as a portable item for relocation."
  },
